  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Cycle 12 on refined_d_cnn_optimized.py / sers_data_3_classes: best trial this cycle achieved HO=0.6115 (CV=0.8793) with num_conv_layers=4, filters=64, learning_rate=0.0001, dropout_rate=0.4 (batch_norm default=0, weight_decay default=0). This exceeds the long-standing 0.4420 ceiling, demonstrating that careful hyperparameter selection can improve HO beyond previous dead-end conclusions. However, the CV-HO gap remains large (~0.27), and the finetune escalation trial failed. Parameter importance earlier in the cycle ranked dropout_rate and learning_rate as top drivers. The architecture still exhibits overfitting but is not entirely futile; further systematic tuning with explicit batch_norm=1 and weight_decay may reduce the gap.", "category": "progress_report", "experiment_name": "refined_d_cnn_optimized.py", "_data_source": "sers_data_3_classes", "_manifest_name": "sers_data_3_classes", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 512, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "representation_type": "1D_CNN"}}</data>
