  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Cycle 13 on refined_d_cnn_optimized.py / sers_data_3_classes: num_conv_layers=5 with dropout_rate=0.3 achieved HO=0.6363 (new record, exceeding 0.6115 baseline), but CV=0.8999 \u2192 CV-HO gap=0.2636 remains severe. Dropout=0.4 degraded HO to 0.5236-0.5971, confirming dropout=0.3 is the sweet spot for this depth. num_conv_layers=4 with dropout=0.4 collapsed to HO=0.4420, showing depth=5 is critical. The finetune pathway (run_training_trial_with_finetune) is still broken with Celery error 'cluster.tasks.run_finetune_training_worker' across two attempts. The Optuna sweep tool has a code bug ('_missing_from_sweep' is not defined). Key insight: 5 conv layers + moderate dropout (0.3) + batch_norm=1 is the best 1D config found, but the persistent ~0.26 gap confirms fundamental overfitting that hyperparameter tuning alone cannot close. The data-leakage audit and 2D/3D representation exploration remain the only viable paths forward.", "category": "progress_report", "experiment_name": "refined_d_cnn_optimized.py", "_data_source": "sers_data_3_classes", "_manifest_name": "sers_data_3_classes", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 512, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 48, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 24, "representation_type": "1D_CNN"}}</data>
